    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #90\n\n- 2026-09-19 01:53Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-19 02:36Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #441 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Confirmed: branch `bb/relay-90-implementation-audit-fixes-20-23-implem-thr_i5m6sp8daz` is pushed to origin at commit `c8146c5`. ## Summary Implements issue #90 — structured mail read and flag search. The mail-query parser (`backend/packages/data/src/mail/search.ts`) now supports `is:read`, `is:unread`, `is:flagged`, and `is:unflagged` operators, compiled directly over issue #97's canonical `read`/`flagged` boolean item properties rather than being left in free text. - Missing `read`/`flagged` properties on legacy rows default to `false` (unread/unflagged), matching `messageFlagProperties`'s own documented default. - Identical repeated operators (`is:unread is:unread`) collapse harmlessly. - Contradictory operators (`is:read is:unread`, or the flagged equivalent) throw a `ValidationError` (`validation_failed`) with `details: { field: 'is:read'|'is:flagged', conflict: [...] }`. - The read and flagged dimensions compose independently with AND, and compose correctly with the existing `from:`/`has:attachment`/`before:`/`after:` operators and free text. Added parser unit tests (contradiction, collapse, composition) and a real-Postgres integration test covering legacy/read/flagged/read+flagged rows and their composition with `from:`. ## Test plan - [x] `pnpm run verify` in `backend/`: lint, format, build, unit, migration-numbering, write-safety, dependency-boundaries, integration (105 files / 1296 tests), e2e (2 files / 9 tests) — all pass - [x] `pnpm run verify` in `web/`: lint, format, build, test (25 files / 195 tests) — all pass (no web changes were needed; this is a backend-only issue) Branch: `bb/relay-90-implementation-audit-fixes-20-23-implem-thr_i5m6sp8daz` 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-19 03:23Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #441 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Confirmed: branch `bb/relay-90-implementation-audit-fixes-20-23-implem-thr_i5m6sp8daz` is pushed to origin at commit `4daad74`. Pushed the review-fix commit (`77f77c0` — unrecognized `is:` values now fall back to free text instead of being silently discarded) to the same branch backing PR #441. The push initially rejected as non-fast-forward because a `develop` merge had landed on the remote branch after my last push; merged that in locally (no conflicts, unrelated files from issue #89's work), re-ran the full `backend/` verify pipeline (112 files / 1457 integration tests + 9 e2e tests, all clean), then pushed the merge commit. Branch: `bb/relay-90-implementation-audit-fixes-20-23-implem-thr_i5m6sp8daz` Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-19 03:32Z — This issue was resolved by #441, which just merged into develop.",
